    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58390,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 230,
        "headingText": "<p>EE6Y &amp; XH0XH6 Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue &amp; Nuchal fibroma</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-23T16:18:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 398,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 231,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58391,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 231,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> nuchal fibroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> collagenosis nuchae.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 399,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 232,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58392,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 232,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 400,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 233,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58393,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 233,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nuchal-type fibroma typically arises in the subcutaneous tissues of the posterior neck, but it can also occur at other sites {7872429; 9921988}. Most extranuchal tumours are located on the upper back, but tumours can also arise on the face and extremities.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 401,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 234,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58394,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 234,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>As many as 50% of patients with nuchal-type fibroma have diabetes mellitus {9921988}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 402,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 235,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58395,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 235,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nuchal-type fibroma is significantly more common in men, with a peak incidence in the fourth and fifth decades of life.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 403,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 236,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58396,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 236,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 404,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 237,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58397,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 237,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58398,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The mean tumour size is 3&nbsp;cm. Nuchal-type fibroma is ill defined and has a firm consistency and a white cut surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58399,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nuchal-type fibroma is a poorly circumscribed and paucicellular lesion composed of bland spindle cells, thick haphazardly arranged collagen fibres, and entrapped subcutaneous adipose tissue. Elastic fibres and small blood vessels are present between the collagen fibres. Many nuchal-type fibromas contain a localized proliferation of small nerves, in some cases similar to those seen in traumatic neuroma. This feature is usually absent from Gardner fibroma, which is often otherwise indistinguishable from nuchal-type fibroma. Compared with normal tissue from the nuchal area, nuchal-type fibroma shows similarly thick collagen fibres. However, in nuchal-type fibroma there is an expansion of collagenized dermis with encasement of adnexa, effacement of the subcutis with entrapment of adipocytes, and (in many cases) extension into underlying skeletal muscle. By immunohistochemistry, the spindled fibroblasts are CD34-positive and negative for &beta;-catenin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58400,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
